# Sol plan / canon / protected-text audit — Movement 2, “No Sanction”

## Verdict — REPAIR

The movement's structure, calendar, entry seam, money, fragment logic, and most protected wording can be ratified. Repair is confined to: (a) one **OWNER-PENDING** protected date for which neither the source nor Books 1–7 supplies a value; (b) restoration of three source-complete protected units or speaker assignments; (c) converting Vastin's invented original cut leaf back to the packet's **page**, because “the leaf does not appear” in this movement; (d) removing facts beyond the four facts Vastin may add about the sub-layer; (e) removing an unplanned disagreement between two counts; and (f) correcting the completion-report count, receipt, and closing log (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:47–69`; `BOOK_MAP.md:60–65,333–353,393`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:171–183`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–173`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:51–53,237–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:7–11,49–65,111–169,191,293–295`). The exact repairs are listed after §8. No broad rewrite is warranted.

## 1. Continuity with the closed text

### Entry seam

- **PASS — place, party, money and day.** The closed text leaves six people at Lowmarch with 118 marks on the 268th and closes on the 270th (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:221–231,285–295`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:191–205`). Movement 2 opens there on the 271st, still with six and with Oryn at the board, and explicitly retains 118 marks (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:3,53–71`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–153`).
- **PASS — bodies.** Lira's ankle was mended and her arm released on day 266, with the arm slow for a month, wet-aching for a year and not to be fallen on (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127–151`; `BOOK_MAP.md:214–218`). On day 273 she uses both arms, hears the arm once, does not stop, and falls beside it rather than on it (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–5,61–111`). Brom's right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; she tests it and declines to undo it (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:145–149`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:173–183`).
- **PASS — counts and objects.** Deployment enters at twenty-nine (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:205–215`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:193`); the second wand enters at forty notches on day 270 and reaches forty-one on day 271 (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:285–289`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:41–43`). The kit cord remains twenty strides, four knots at five-stride intervals, with no yardage assigned to a cord (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:9–13`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:195`). Karis retains the case, fifty-two sheets, map, instruments, stored hair and unread index (`STATE_LEDGER.md:198`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–235`). “West”, “Treswick” and “Deepstacks” were spoken together at the day-268 table (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:251–259`); nobody says *west* in the back room (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–239`).
- **PASS — stake marks.** This movement mentions the dead surveyor's four-sign index with stake thirty-two and assigns no stroke/bar to stakes thirty-one or thirty-three; the fourth site's thirty-four is not restaged (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:229–235`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:10,17`).
- **PASS — restriction.** Closed Movement 1 says the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district and is served within the hour (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:257–259`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:205`). Seln and Vastin give the same trigger and service time (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:79–105`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:75–79`).

### Vastin against locked Books 6 and 7

- Locked Book 6 gives a plain grey coat, empty hands, a complete reading of the case, the sentence “I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be,” refusal to verify/report/certify, “forty years” as career, and “No. I am not with anyone” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:139–175,189–221`). Book 6 later shows the pending restriction and his unannotated return of the summary (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-58.md:49–53,59–105`). Locked Book 7 gives only a courtesy-copy window: he reads the completion report twice, cannot explain its arrival, and returns it unannotated (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-44.md:141`; `book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:104,118,682`).
- **PASS.** Movement 2 states no age; “forty years” is Vastin's own rounding (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:181,251`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:85,247`). He shows no Iron Wall: the ferry is held by a turn around a post, boots, back and hands, and the narration expressly finds no grey or declaration (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:115–129`). He never sees the directive or objection, never learns the integration mechanism, never computes the technician's date, never asks to join, and is not framed as joining (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:129–131`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:19–23`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–151,223–239`). Cael remembers rather than reprints the Book 6 sentence and says only the required line (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:95–99`; locked wording at `book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:189–191`).
- **REPAIR — extra sub-layer provenance.** The mender's training, damp-frame anecdote, service schedules and history of failed attempts add more than the four permitted facts (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–173` versus `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:65–68`). Retain only: unreachable/no key, citation, suppressed records, technician's line. Exact fixes 5–11 do that.

### Records, objects, knowledge and sums

- **REPAIR — records.** The flat has six years, six rows, “More than four”, and the completion report as the last loose sheet (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–11`; `BOOK_MAP.md:62`). “Six rows” and “six years” do not themselves require that a row represent a site rather than a year; the next packet only requires a “second row” (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:32`). The plan's anomaly column contains *Total* (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:51`; `BOOK_MAP.md:62`), but the draft turns *Total* into a footer before a numeric figure (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:237–241`). Fixes 44–45 restore it as the repeated anomaly-column entry and remove the number. The disagreement between that invented figure and Karis's sign-group count is likewise not in the plan and would create a new Movement 3 mystery (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:241–253`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:95,150`); cut it by fix 15. The last sheet currently prints five names but omits the locked count of six (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:11` versus `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-43.md:47–53` and `chapter-40.md:231`); add it by fix 16. The Book 7 report's “No price paid” is not repeated here, but no contrary price is introduced (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-40.md:231`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:7–17`).
- **REPAIR — page/leaf identity.** The packet calls this document a page and expressly says “The leaf does not appear” (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:52,67`); the map reserves “the leaf” for the day-293 chamber reading (`BOOK_MAP.md:333,352`). The draft instead makes this an original leaf cut from a bound register (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:197`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:49–63,169`). Amend the carrier to Vastin's copied page without touching the protected line (fixes 1, 12, 17–29, 31, 33–35, 37–43 and 46).
- **REPAIR — custody statements.** Karis has already turned the top row, read the completion report, read the page and copied the technician's sheet (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:221–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–15,59–91,109–135`). Therefore “Examined by nobody” in the receipt and “has read none of them” in the log contradict the same chapter (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:169,293`). Fixes 33 and 43 say exactly what remains unfinished.
- **PASS — fragments.** The only earnest fragment use is the Iron read of the landing bank (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:63–95,147–149`), logged as deployment thirty twice (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Pressure, Anchor and Wind are refused at the landing (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:63–71`); Wind and the read are refused in Lira's bout (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:13–15,95–99`); Tide is not used on Oryn's patients or Vastin (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:167–171`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:43–47`); Shadow is held and sealed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:259–263`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:191–199`). Oryn does not read Cael (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:43–47`). The cut-page Blade prompt is unnecessary and disappears with fix 18.
- **PASS — money.** The crew's purse is still 118 marks on day 276 and stays in Brom's hand because the cordage does not cross (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–167`). Vastin's own purse pays one copper ferry fare, a copper and a half for bread, one copper for a bowl and one copper for the loft: four and a half coppers (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:161–167,239–247`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:41–47,263–271`). The copper on Ephram's letter is Cael's separate posting coin and is never drawn from Brom's purse (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:141–145`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–137`). Movement-end crew purse: **118 marks**; this is an inference from the explicit held purse and absence of any crew withdrawal.

## 2. Movement plan and every owner flag

The packet beats occur in order: week and Oryn's bench (`chapter-07.md:3–183`); Teague's preparation and Lira's bout (`chapter-07.md:187–243`; `chapter-08.md:3–135`); ferry at first light (`chapter-09.md:3–203`); plank (`chapter-09.md:207–265`); long table (`chapter-10.md:3–283`; `chapter-11.md:3–125`); Vastin with nothing to do (`chapter-11.md:129–187`); records, page, sheet, stairs and hand-width close (`chapter-11.md:191–259`; `chapter-12.md:3–299`). The withheld matters remain withheld except for the extra layer provenance and the original-leaf substitution identified in §1 (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:61–69`).

Seln teaches nobody in the progression sense: his gate and routing-note speeches explain documents already in the room, while no drill, doctrine or one-to-one instruction occurs (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:75–105`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:23–31`). Removing the two invented intelligence anecdotes at `manuscript/chapter-10.md:97–99` also preserves the packet's explicit hold for his first teaching at the Movement 3 spring (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:69`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:32,37`).

Every `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:144–159` flag is ruled as follows:

1. **Deployment 29 → 30 — KEEP.** The packet locks twenty-nine only at Movement 2 entry (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:16`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:193,205`), and neither the map nor Movement 3 fixes a post-landing count (`BOOK_MAP.md:60–65`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). The new landing read is earnest and pays with near sight (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:71–95,147–149,263–265`). The source ferry uses no fragment (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md:3–39`), but the packet gives the edition author the flood landing's mechanics (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:57,73`). Keep thirty.
2. **Compact-date marker — OWNER-PENDING, blocking final ratification.** The source does not print a value; it says only “and a date”, then describes a registry year and day (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:97–101`). The map likewise has `[a Compact date]` (`BOOK_MAP.md:353`). No exact date can be restored without minting canon; see §5 and fix 30.
3. **Karis's “Under every station…” — KEEP verbatim, remove gloss.** Locked Book 6 says the first memorandum went to every station and that the reading is older than the function by an unknown span (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-39.md:105,117`). It does not literally establish the protected sentence's continental claim. The map nevertheless makes the B7-reconciled wording binding and owner-pending (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:49`; `BOOK_MAP.md:393`). The exact line at `manuscript/chapter-10.md:149` stays; explanatory expansion at `:153–155,173` goes.
4. **Speaker assignments.** “Archmarshal” belongs to Cael in the source and is correct (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md:29–35`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:179–183`). “What follows you” belongs to Lira, not Seln (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md:133–139`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:51–53`): amend. “More than four” belongs to Karis and is correct (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:37–41`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:239–245`). “Don't take the stairs fast” belongs to Oryn, not Karis (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:129–133`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:187–191`): amend with the full source unit. Karis's preceding council question is hers in the source and may remain expanded (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md:145–151`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:99–105`).
5. **“More than four” without a printed number — KEEP; CUT the number and disagreement.** The plan requires the qualitative line and *Total* as the anomaly-column entry, not a numeric footer or a clash of two counts (`BOOK_MAP.md:62`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:51`). The source also withholds the number because Karis has not checked it (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:27–45`). After fixes 15 and 44–45, Movement 3 inherits no unexplained clerk/Karis mismatch.
6. **Rope — KEEP.** The first ferry carries people and no goods; the cordage stays on the far bank and 118 remains available (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:29–33`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–145`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–167`).
7. **Progression vocabulary — ACCEPT.** The movement teaches registry machinery rather than padding with trials (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:41,152`); the one new earnest read is fully priced (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:63–95,147–149`). Movement 3 already carries the next dense teaching at the cut and spring (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31–32`).
8. **Teague's road — KEEP OPEN, inherit explicitly.** He has forty sacks on the bank and an after-thaw road term, but the movement does not establish whether he leaves before the morning slip (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:255`). Movement 3 must choose his day-278 placement without contradicting those facts.
9. **Classification-event definition — CUT.** “Any occasion”, the examples, and “thousands” are not in the plan, exceed the four-new-facts ceiling, and make the hidden date easier to connect (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:123–125`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:65–66`). Fix 32 leaves Vastin unable to identify the event.
10. **Orders/stairs — KEEP the walk-back mechanics; repair the speaker.** Vastin walks the order back twice, starts fast, stops and climbs slowly (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:193–219`), satisfying the Millrace sequence lock. Restore Oryn's source line by fix 36.
11. **Oryn's swallowed sentence — KEEP.** It remains unspoken on the 268th, 271st and night of the 277th (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:257–265`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:121–125`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:257–261`).
12. **Seln's two inventions — CUT.** Neither the grade-building boast nor Vastin's three cases/two limps is established, and both spend trade history while Seln is to teach nobody (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:95–103`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:69`). Fixes 3–4 retain suspicion without new history.
13. **Sweep probe — ACCEPT after the line repairs.** See §7: exact overlap is entirely protected/packet-quoted; no tracking rewrite is indicated.
14. **`audit-notes.md` — no text ruling.** Its appearance is provenance metadata only (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:159`); this audit neither reads nor alters it.

