**Compact-date ruling.** Books 4–5 retain protected named dates such as “the eleventh of Sowing”, “the nineteenth of Reaping” and “the twentieth of Reaping” (`book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-37.md:49,221`; `chapter-52.md:193`; `book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-13.md:127`) under OWNER #35. Season-blind Book 6 uses ordinal forms such as “the eighth day of the year”, “the first day of the year” and numbered First-/Fifth-days (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-05.md:3`; `chapter-07.md:93`; `chapter-10.md:15`), but **no Book 1–7 manuscript prints a Compact registry year-and-day date of this type**. There is therefore no value and no like-format precedent to reconcile. Fix 30 changes the misleading Tier-B marker to an explicit OWNER-PENDING marker. Once the owner supplies the exact registry year and day, the publishable three-line join must be:

`*Deep layer. Sequence initiated — [OWNER-SUPPLIED COMPACT DATE].*\n\n*Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —*`

The placeholder is not protected wording and cannot be ratified as final prose. No protected document is otherwise printed twice (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:105–109,239–245`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:65,111–133`).

## 6. New canon minted

Rulings correspond one-for-one to `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:125–142`.

1. **Ferry rig — KEEP.** It is within the author's flood-landing ownership and creates no later conflict (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:5–23,45–61,151–153`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:57,73`).
2. **First boat — KEEP.** Eight passengers, no goods, improvised repairs and the later foot crossing do not conflict with the map (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:29–33,127–143`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–145`).
3. **Week's water/tent figures — KEEP.** They fit days 271–276 and the day-277 ferry (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:3–39`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:139–167`; `BOOK_MAP.md:217–218`).
4. **Mule's stool — KEEP.** It pays the six-with-Oryn seam without making her join (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:53–71`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:27–39`).
5. **Gate explanation — KEEP.** Its trigger agrees with locked Book 6 (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:75–117`; `book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-58.md:49–53`).
6. **Oryn's Lowmarch bench — KEEP.** It is expressly author-owned and names no patient (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:135–183`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:45,73`).
7. **New cloth — KEEP.** Teague first and the five held eleventh preserve the closed standing (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:187–211`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:202,205`).
8. **Teague's salt/road term — KEEP, with Movement 3 placement open.** No contradiction; inherit the unresolved departure (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:255`).
9. **Bout — KEEP.** It fulfills the packet exactly: arm speaks once, Lira does not stop, no fragment is used (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–135`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:46`).
10. **Ephram letter — KEEP.** It pays the inherited letter and introduces no name (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:139–145`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–143`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:202`).
11. **Vastin's arrival body/coat/stick/purse/loft — KEEP.** No age is stated and the knee carries forward to the cut (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:171–201,235–267`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:263–271`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31`).
12. **Vastin's road to the papers — AMEND.** Keep no key, citation, suppressed records, completion report, and inability to enter the archive; cut mender biography, frame repair, office schedules and failed-attempt history (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–173,189–225`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:65–68`). Exact fixes 5–11.
13. **Flat — AMEND.** Keep the physical flat, six years, six rows, measures, anomaly-column *Total* and no printed number; remove the invented numerical footer/two-count disagreement and add the locked report's count of six (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:7–11`). Exact fixes 15–16 and 44–45.
14. **Page — AMEND.** Keep a copied page, oilcloth and the protected line; cut the original leaf, binder holes, knife, cut-edge ethics and Blade prompt because the packet withholds the leaf (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:49–95`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:52,67`). Exact fixes 1, 12, 17–29, 31, 33–35, 37–43 and 46.
