## #30 — Between-books items from the Monroe 1.3 Book 1 ending (default in force)
- **The book's last line and the six restored units** (Gault's last note; the personnel query; the waystation board; "You couldn't read me…"; Cael's reply to Daeva; the closing exchange) are verbatim from the protected wording, with only the edition's mandatory changes ("Since my Kindling"; "Nine fragments"; the personnel query's teaching-assistant role, calendar and house frame).
- **The shelf is the SECOND camp beyond the Line and the first fire** — Book 7's plan is amended to match (audit fix 16), not Book 6.

## 47. Book 6 ch49 — the certification minute's "evaluator of record" (coordinator ruling, 2026-10-11)
The protected Tier B minute reads "*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*" In this edition Gault is the evaluator of record and the Archmarshal's office is the certifying office that declined. **Ruling: the protected line stays verbatim and is read as the form's own mislabel** — an old column heading with no place for the right office — which the scene already dramatizes (four pens stop; Gault "had declined nothing"). One plain sentence was added outside the protected line so a young reader is told so directly: "The refusal was the Archmarshal's; the form's old column had only Gault's title to put it under." Owner may instead release the protected line and have it name the certifying office.

## 48. Book 7 reconciliation to edition Book 6 (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
Source: `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md`, `B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md` (Sol) and `B6-RECONCILIATION-COORDINATOR-OVERRIDES.md`. Defaults in force until the owner rules:
- **Season-blind and feet/yards, continued into Book 7** (as #37 O1 and #42 did for Books 5 and 6). Named seasons and metric units are replaced, minimally, INCLUDING inside Book 7's protected lines (for example "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." becomes "After the thaw. …"; "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." becomes the same distance in yards). Generic "season" and "month" stay. Every changed protected line is listed, old and new, in `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md`; the owner may restore any or all when the series calendar is ruled.
- **Time since Kindling** (#18 extended to Book 7): the protected first pole "I've spent four years being the case the instruments couldn't parse" reads "Since my Kindling I've been the case…".
- **The birthday:** day 102 past the Line stands, never beside a season, a month order or a count back to the last birthday. By the edition's own day counts the two birthdays fall roughly 225 days apart (Book 6's mid-year, the year's close near day 207, then 102 days). The prose never states it; the series calendar remains the owner's to rule (#35, #42).
- **The shelf** is the second camp past the Line and the first fire (#46). **The Velmere letter** stays sealed on Brom's table at Halcenvane; it is not carried. **Seln's case** came east in his own satchel and rides under the canvas from the shelf.
- **Shadow's first Book 7 use** is restaged so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (audit B2). **#23** (sell the cart and gelding in Lowmarch's first week; the money is a sealed reserve) is treated as binding.

## 49. Book 7 — protected Quiet-line / Kindling wording (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 4)
Seven protected lines say variants of "mine didn't", "my Path", "mine has been asleep since I was fourteen", "dark since fourteen", "every Path … his had not". Edition canon (Book 6): Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and the Arbiter went dark; he has no Path. At a Quiet line the others' live Arbiters stop, his is dark before and after, and his fragments still answer. **Default until ruled: the protected lines stay verbatim**, the surrounding plan and prose state the canon, and the lines read as Cael's own shorthand. Options: (1) release only the conflicting clauses for a minimal canon repair; (2) release the affected log entries for clean re-composition; (3) keep as is (the default).

**#49 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 4).** Read closely, most of the seven lines already agree with canon as written: the first says the others' ARBITERS stopped and "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen."; the fourth says "whatever I am isn't a Path"; Karis's struck line says "one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line". Only two use "Path … mine" loosely ("Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't"; "every Path in this camp stops, and mine doesn't"). Default confirmed: all seven stay verbatim as Cael's log shorthand; Movement 4's packet carries a binding note that narration and dialogue never say "his Path" and state the canon exactly (the five live Arbiters stop; his has been dark since Kindling; the fragments still answer). If the owner prefers, only those two clauses need releasing.

## 50. Book 7 — "Six years I've wanted a face" (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 7)
The protected line gives Seln six years; edition Book 6 has him carry the case twelve years (fifteen in service). **Default until ruled: the line stays verbatim** and the plan stops calling the case a six-year matter. Options: (1) "Twelve years I've wanted a face."; (2) "All these years I've wanted a face."; (3) keep six and name a separate event six years back that began the wish.

**#50 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 7).** Default confirmed and written into Movement 7's packet: the line stays verbatim and unglossed; no six-year event is invented; the case's twelve years is not stated in that scene. One thing the owner may like to know: the closed Movement 5 has Seln date the registry's survey of the circles at "five years ago by the stake, maybe six" (ch34), so on the page "six years" can be heard as the time since that survey without any change. If the owner prefers option (1) or (2), it is a one-numeral change.

## 51. Book 7 — "Tomorrow makes three" (OWNER ITEM; coordinator default in force, 2026-10-11)
The protected second pole closes Movement 6 (ch44, written at the well as day 111 breaks): "…We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." On this edition's calendar "tomorrow" is day 112, a road to Lowmarch's board; the next quiet ground entered is the Stair on day 114. The count is also arguable: the six have gone in at the Fallow once as a party (day 96), or twice if the first crossings at the line are counted. Sol's audit found no honest gloss. **Default until ruled: the line stays word for word, where the plan places it, unglossed.** Options: (1) keep as is (the default); (2) keep the words and move the entry to the night of day 113, the eve of the Stair, where "tomorrow" is true (Movement 6 would then close on Oryn's leaving); (3) supply replacement wording. Options 2 and 3 change published chapters.
- Related, NOT an owner item: the restored protected line "I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board" beside Oryn at Millrace (one day south of Lowmarch) on day 113 was resolved by the owner on 2026-09-04 (EXC-B7-003: "her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days"; BOOK_MAP lists it under "do not reopen"). Movement 7's packet carries a binding note.

## 52–55. Book 8 — owner items from the early plan audit (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
Source: `book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md` §F (Sol). The audit is early: Book 7's last two movements were still open, and it is re-run when they close. Defaults below hold until the owner rules; each protected line stays word for word.
- **#52 (needed before Book 8 Movement 3).** Karis's protected "right for five years or wrong for five years". Book 7 never states her hypothesis and gives it no five-year history. **Default:** the line stays verbatim as Karis's own rounding; narration does not treat five years as a fact. Options: (1) the owner confirms an older private conviction, five years old, distinct from the Book 7 hypothesis; (2) release the clause for wording without a number; (3) the default.
- **#53 (needed before Book 8 Movement 4).** Protected "it took four years and a hearing to walk out". The plan itself notes the figure does not fit the academy span; #18 bars numbers for time since Kindling, and Book 7's first pole was amended on that ground. **Default:** verbatim, as Cael's rough spoken figure, never repeated as fact. Options: (1) the default; (2) release only "four years" for wording without a number, as was done for Book 7's first pole; (3) settle the series calendar so that it is true.
- **#54 (needed before Book 8 Movement 9).** The plan has the young member of Teague's crew named aloud once at his death. The edition has never named Teague's crew and no name is owner-approved. **Default:** no name is minted: the cry is narrated by its effect and the name's sound is not rendered. Options: (1) the owner supplies a name before Movement 9 (it then goes in the registry and the pronunciation list); (2) the default; (3) he stays unnamed even in-world.
- **#55 (needed before Book 8 Movement 9).** "Tell Lira's family I said so" (Cael's last letter to Hesk) still has no setup; this is #25, still open. **Default:** verbatim, no setup added. Options: confirm the opaque line; authorize one earlier setup beat; release or remove the clause.

## 56–58. Book 8 — three more protected-text items from the final plan re-run (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
Source: `book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-H-RERUN.md` (Sol) and `B7-RECONCILIATION-COORDINATOR-OVERRIDES.md`. Sol's list proposed new wording for these protected lines; the coordinator held them back, because no standing decision covers them. Each stays word for word until the owner rules.
- **#56 (Book 8 Movement 2 or 3, Thornwater).** `"Five months and twenty days."` — Lira's arm, from the Ring to its release. It is true on the plan's day count (day 96 to day 265–266) but only if a month is thirty days, and #35 says the prose never states month lengths. **Default:** verbatim. Options: keep; "A hundred and seventy days."; or a wording without a figure.
- **#57 (Book 8 Movements 8–9; extends #49).** Three protected lines speak of Cael's "Path" or say the machine never lit for him: `Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died.`; `His Path did not die. It also did not notice it should have.` (narration); `a machine that lit for everyone but him` (narration). Edition canon since Book 6: he has no Path; his own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, and it went dark. **Default:** verbatim; nothing else in the book says "his Path". The two narration lines are the hardest to square, since they are not Cael's own shorthand. Options: release the clauses for a minimal canon repair (Sol drafted wording, kept in the re-run report); or keep as is.
- **#58 (Book 8 Movement 9).** "the whole year" in three protected places (`I've spent the whole year wanting`; `He had spent the whole year learning`; the plan's note beside them). The audit finds a whole year impossible on the plan's own day spine. **Default:** verbatim, as a rough figure. Options: keep; "all these days"; or settle the series calendar.
Applied under standing decisions, and listed old and new in `B7-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md` so any can be restored: Book 8's named seasons (#48) and its three "five years" counts since Kindling (#18), the same changes Books 5–7 made.

## 59. Book 8 — Teague's spear: "the tall woman" (source) or "a tall man" (locked Book 7) (coordinator default, 2026-10-11)
The source's Book 8 makes Teague's spear-carrier a tall woman throughout. The edition's locked Book 7 wrote this unnamed person as a man in five places (ch25:85 "a man with a spear"; ch51:357; ch52:45, :335, :337), because Book 7's plan never gave a gender and nobody caught it against Book 8. Book 8's protected text (§10) contains no gendered reference to the spear, and Book 8 Movement 1 uses no pronoun.
**Default in force: Book 8 follows the locked Book 7 — a tall man** — as the edition followed its own earlier books in #1 (Pellin) and #7 (Bracken). No locked text changes and no protected text changes.
**Option:** restore the source's tall woman by changing those five places in Book 7 (about ten words) and re-binding Book 7 (new hashes, a reissued DIRECTOR_CUT_READY, a republish), then reverting the Book 8 plan marks. Needed before Book 8 Movement 2 gives this person a pronoun; later is possible but costs more to undo.
Also settled from the same audit, without owner action: Teague CAN read (Book 7's protected line has him read a slip twice; Book 8's plan said he could not); the stroke and bar is on stakes thirty-two and thirty-four only; the court is about fifty cords across, not 159 (159 of Book 7's cords would be about 3,500 yards, against the plan's own 1,107).

> **Update 2026-10-11 (Book 8 Movement 2, #59):** from chapter 7 the edition gives Teague's spear-carrier "he/his" on the page (ch7:215, ch8:7/37/87/127, ch9:91), following the default (a tall man, as in locked Book 7). Choosing "the tall woman" now means re-touching those Book 8 lines as well as re-binding Book 7.

## 60. Book 8 Movement 2 — the technician's sheet: the Compact date is not printed (default in force; not blocking)
The protected unit (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 5) reads "Deep layer. Sequence initiated" [a Compact date] "Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —". The source prints no value either ("She gave the date. It was a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it"). Sol's plan audit asked for an owner-supplied date. **Coordinator default:** the edition does as the source does — the sheet shows a date in the office's reckoning and the page never gives its figures, in Movement 2 or at the spring in Movement 3 (where Cael knows it for his Kindling day; no span of years is computed, #18). If the owner wants a printed registry date, it has to be minted and reconciled with #35/#42 (the series calendar), and ch12 and the spring scene re-touched.

