grep -Fxc \"The wide door of the second building stood a hand's breadth open. He went as far as that door, and looked in at a plate lying in the floor under its frame, brown as an old coin, with dust on it. He had put his name for forty years to the protocol that governed every such plate. He had once carried a plate up a bluff, with a file and a set of questions, to a boy, and all three had told him nothing; and when the form came round that would have had the boy read a second time, he had declined. He had never told the boy why. He drew the door to, as he had found it, and went back into the house.\" editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-08.md
