editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-10.md:191:"I looked for the office's account of its own beginnings, as you would have. It keeps registers of the housings, back to the first that were ever built, and in the oldest of those that I was let to see there is a line for the layer. Where a maker's name ought to stand upon that line, there is none. There is a citation. It gives a word which I had never seen used as it is used there, and it sends its reader elsewhere for the whole of the matter."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-10.md:201:It was nine days since a small pale woman had laid her palm on a strip of oilcloth and said that town's name for the first time in his hearing. She had come to it from the east, off fifty-two sheets of rubbed stone and a dead man's ledger. This man had come to it from the other side, out of the Compact's own house, down a stair and through a frame shop. Neither had known that the other was on the road.
