editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-07.md:171:He was aware of the tenth of his own fragments while he watched. Tide did not stir, since it had never asked for anything; but it lay in him, a piece out of a healer's Path, partial and Iron, and he knew exactly what it would do. Two fingers on that child's wrist and a count of ten would have shown him where her breath stuck, and would have mended nothing. He had a rule against so much as asking, unless there were a purpose, and he saw for the first time how thin a thing he owned. She had the reading and the mending together, and he had been handed the ruler without the saw.

